        "data": {
          "homepage": "https://www.arte.tv/en/videos/120440-000-A/the-great-smog-of-london/",
          "overview": "For five days in December 1952, a thick smog suffocated the British capital causing the death of thousands of Londoners. The health catastrophe lead to a realisation, in Britain and around the world, that air pollution was a serious threat to human health. This documentary reveals what happened, hour by hour, in one of the worst peacetime disasters of the 20th century.",
